  "result": "The 30-minute lesson on context and memory (O3) is written at `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html`. I couldn't render or open the page in this session, so the interactive checks haven't been tried in a browser.\n\nEach concept starts from a traced makerspace example, then gets its name, a \"Why this works\" box and a check:\n1. **The context window:** a request built field by field, with a token tally, and why every part of it costs money.\n2. **What is kept between steps:** the program resends the whole history on every call, so billing is the sum of the calls.\n3. **When it fills:** context rot, clearing old tool results, summarizing, and the 400 error you get if you do nothing.\n4. **Notes between sessions:** a `memory/sam.md` file, with a warning that a note is not a verified record, so the booking code must check the training record itself.\n5. **Retrieval:** search, then read one page, instead of loading all the manuals.\n\nIt ends with a worked example for Sam and a partly blank one for Priya.\n\n- **Review rounds:** I ran the review loop twice and stopped at the cap, so the second round's remaining findings are not re-checked. The details are in `review-records/0001-lesson.md`.\n- **Open points:** I declined splitting section 3, which still holds two techniques. Wrong answers explain the reason straight away rather than giving a hint first. Neither figure shows the \"resent versus new\" split.\n- **Length:** the lesson is about 4,900 words, roughly 33 minutes at 150 words a minute, which is inside the allowed range.\n- **Stray file:** `drafts/0001-plan.md.promises-note` is left over from the planner and I couldn't delete it without a shell. It is unused.\n- **Workspace files:** I created `RESOURCES.md` with the three sources and added a line about this lesson to `NOTES.md`.\n\nAsk me for a quiz on it when you're ready, or ask me anything about it.",
